# Mathua CAT Diagnostic  --  Binary Search on Concept Graph

direction: down

Start: Start Diagnostic\nGet all concepts (topo-sorted)\nSet Low=0, High=N-1

Loop: Binary Search Loop {
  Mid: Compute Midpoint\nPos = Low + (High-Low)/2

  Question: Generate Question\nfor concept at Pos

  Answer: Student Answers\nwithin time limit

  Decision: Evaluate\ncorrect + fast enough?
}

Correct: Correct\nMove forward\nLow = Pos + 1

Incorrect: Incorrect/Slow\nMove backward\nHigh = Pos - 1

Check: Streak Check\nX correct in a row?

Result: Frontier Located\nEstimate approx position\nRecord mastery for all passed

Done: Diagnostic Complete\nMerge with existing progress\nOptimistic merge

# Flow
Start -> Loop
Loop -> Mid
Mid -> Question
Question -> Answer
Answer -> Decision
Decision -> Correct: Yes
Decision -> Incorrect: No
Correct -> Check
Incorrect -> Loop: reset streak
Check -> Loop: No, continue
Check -> Result: Yes, X in a row
Check -> Result: Hit boundaries
Result -> Done

# Side note
Note: "Key Parameters: midpoint topo-DAG to binary search, ~20-35 questions"

# Styling
nodes: {
  style: {
    font-size: 12
    border-radius: 6
  }
}

edges: {
  style: {
    stroke: "#6b6a64"
    font-size: 10
  }
}
